  "title": "India's Cotton Imports and Duty-Free Policy",
  "summary": "The Indian government plans to extend duty-free cotton imports until December to ease supply pressures during the lean season, while the projected decline in cotton production could prompt the government to consider extending duty-free imports as output may fall 12-18%.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "India's cotton production is projected to decline to around 29 million bales in 2026-27.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The government waived the 11% customs duty on cotton imports for five months from June 1 through October 31.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The extension aims to ease supply pressures during the lean season.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
